{title: Crown Him with Many Crowns}
{artist: Matthew Bridges (1800-1894) & Godfrey Thring (1823-1903)}
{key: D}
{copyright: Public Domain}

{sov: Verse 1}
[D]Crown Him with [Bm]many crowns, the [G]Lamb upon His [A]throne;
[D]Hark! how the [Bm]heavenly anthem drowns all [E]music but its [A]own.
[D]Awake, my [G]soul, and sing of [E]Him who died for [A]thee,
And [D]hail Him [G]as thy [D]matchless King through [G]all e[A]terni[D]ty.
{eov}

{sov: Verse 2}
[D]Crown Him the [Bm]Lord of love! Be[G]hold His hands and [A]side,
[D]Those wounds, yet [Bm]visible above, in [E]beauty glori[A]fied.
[D]No angel [G]in the sky can [E]fully bear that [A]sight,
But [D]downward [G]bends his [D]wondering eye at [G]mysteries [A]so [D]bright.
{eov}

{sov: Verse 3}
[D]Crown Him the [Bm]Lord of peace, whose [G]power a scepter [A]sways
[D]From pole to [Bm]pole, that wars may cease, ab[E]sorbed in prayer and [A]praise.
[D]His reign shall [G]know no end, and [E]round His pierced [A]feet
Fair [D]flowers of [G]paradise [D]extend their [G]fragrance [A]ever [D]sweet.
{eov}

{sov: Verse 4}
[D]Crown Him the [Bm]Lord of years, the [G]Potentate of [A]time,
[D]Creator [Bm]of the rolling spheres, in[E]effably sub[A]lime.
[D]All hail, Re[G]deemer, hail! For [E]Thou hast died for [A]me;
Thy [D]praise and [G]glory [D]shall not fail through[G]out e[A]terni[D]ty.
{eov}
